# Firecracker API Calls
#
# These are the exact HTTP requests that the SDK makes over the Unix socket.
# You can't run these from a REST client directly (they need --unix-socket),
# but this documents the API contract.
#
# Start firecracker first:
#   rm -f /tmp/fc-demo.sock
#   firecracker --api-sock /tmp/fc-demo.sock --no-seccomp &
#
# Then use curl to send these requests:
#   curl -s --unix-socket /tmp/fc-demo.sock http://localhost/<path>

### 1. Set machine config (vCPUs + memory)
PUT http://localhost/machine-config
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vcpu_count": 2,
  "mem_size_mib": 512
}

### 2. Set boot source (kernel + args)
PUT http://localhost/boot-source
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kernel_image_path": "/opt/fc/vmlinux",
  "boot_args": "console=ttyS0 reboot=k panic=1 pci=off root=/dev/vda rw"
}

### 3. Attach root filesystem as virtio block device
PUT http://localhost/drives/rootfs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "drive_id": "rootfs",
  "path_on_host": "/opt/fc/rootfs.ext4",
  "is_root_device": true,
  "is_read_only": false
}

### 4. Configure logging
PUT http://localhost/logger
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "log_path": "/tmp/fc-demo.log",
  "level": "Info",
  "show_level": true,
  "show_log_origin": true
}

### 5. Boot the VM (this is where KVM_RUN happens)
PUT http://localhost/actions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action_type": "InstanceStart"
}

### 6. Check machine config (while running)
GET http://localhost/machine-config

### 7. Check VM state (while running)
GET http://localhost/vm

### 8. Graceful shutdown (CtrlAltDel → guest init handles it)
PUT http://localhost/actions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action_type": "SendCtrlAltDel"
}

### --- Snapshot workflow (after VM is booted and ready) ---

### 9. Pause the VM before snapshotting
PATCH http://localhost/vm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "state": "Paused"
}

### 10. Create a full snapshot
PUT http://localhost/snapshot/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "snapshot_type": "Full",
  "snapshot_path": "/tmp/fc-snapshot",
  "mem_file_path": "/tmp/fc-memory"
}

### 11. Resume after snapshot (if you want to keep using this VM)
PATCH http://localhost/vm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "state": "Resumed"
}

### --- To restore from snapshot, start a NEW firecracker process: ---
# firecracker --restore-from-snapshot /tmp/fc-snapshot --api-sock /tmp/fc-restored.sock
